Z||000000||fieromillie||05-18-2001||01:45 PM||||Hi<BR>Purchased a Yellow Michigan Lemon last month from Ebay. Not at all as stated. Managed to get it home over 400 Miles away. Burned 7 quarts of oil on the way. Checked compression and it was great. First trip out of the driveway and it broke down. Drove about 50 miles great and then started backfiring through the carbrator and losing power till it just stopped. Had it towed home. I can hear the fuel pump kick on. But when I start it will not stay running and is still backfiring through the carbrator. Any suggestions would really be appreciated. Thanks   ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mr.Frosty||05-18-2001||01:49 PM||||Sounds like the timing is way off.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top-Sold <BR>85 GT Turbo-project car||||reg||11
Z||000002||mrfixit58||05-18-2001||01:54 PM||||First off, welcome to the forum. You'll find plenty of advice here but, in order to speed up the analysis of your problem, we need more information.<P>Can you give more info on what type of motor and the year and make of your car? Is is a four or six cylinder? Carburetor? I believe all Fieros came with throttle body injection or, in the case of the six cylinder motors, multi-port fuel injection. I'm not an expert but the more information you give, the easier it will be for someone to assist you.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||05-18-2001||01:55 PM||||88? If so check for platnium plugs DIS ignition hates them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos_1.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mr.Frosty||05-18-2001||02:01 PM||||The way it's sputtering sounds like the notorius pick-up coil in the distributer.Check for fuel pressure if you haven't already,then check for spark.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top-Sold <BR>85 GT Turbo-project car||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieromillie||05-18-2001||02:30 PM||||Sorry, New to this, It is an 84 with a 2.5L TBI, 4 Cyl  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieromillie:<BR><B>Hi<BR>Purchased a Yellow Michigan Lemon last month from Ebay. Not at all as stated. Managed to get it home over 400 Miles away. Burned 7 quarts of oil on the way. Checked compression and it was great. First trip out of the driveway and it broke down. Drove about 50 miles great and then started backfiring through the carbrator and losing power till it just stopped. Had it towed home. I can hear the fuel pump kick on. But when I start it will not stay running and is still backfiring through the carbrator. Any suggestions would really be appreciated. Thanks   </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||84Bill||05-18-2001||02:54 PM||||Yep prolly the Ignition module or P/U coil||||reg||1
Z||000007||deceler8||05-18-2001||03:59 PM||||Seven quarts of oil in 400 miles ?<P>Be thankful it didn't catch fire on the way.<P>Unlikely it's burning all that oil...I'm guessing massive leaks, especially valve cover gasket. All that oil has to go somewhere...it's possible it's in your distributor cap and all over your plug wires.<P>The ignition module is a possibility, but I'd check all of the above before you do anything else.<P>And if your plugs themselves are caked and coated with carbon and oil...drive it back where you got it, drain out the coolant, put about 10 quarts of oil in it, and leave it in neutral with a brick holding down the gas pedal.<P>All this, of course, after the check clears.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ken Wittlief||05-18-2001||04:03 PM||||7 quarts of oil in 400 miles?! a quart an hour at hiway speeds?!<BR> <BR> is it really buring it or is it leaking out somewhere?<P>  If you are actually burning 2 quarts of oil to a tank of gas:<P>  1. Your plugs are totally fouled out.<P>  2. your rings are shot or your valve guides are leaking like a sieve.<P>  you can check the rings by doing a compression test. If you have low compression or fouled plugs, or are burning that much oil, the ECM will not be able to make the engine run right.<P>  Which car did you get on ebay, the one in tenn or the one in hudson, NY? If your compression is low, or if its buring oil that bad sounds like you need to rebuild/replace the motor.<P>maybe its only an oil leak. If you let the car idle does it make a puddle in the driveway? ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ken Wittlief||05-18-2001||04:07 PM||||Is the oil leaking into the coolant? Does your antifreeze look like scummy mud soup? (gotta look under the thermostat cap, not in the overflow bottle)||||reg||1
Z||000010||fieromillie||05-18-2001||05:53 PM||||The oil is blowing out the tailpipe. When sitting idle it is not leaking even a drip of oil onto the driveway.The compression is consistent at 120. The ignition control module has just checked out fine. It will start and just keep backfiring up into the carbrator. It will then cut off. You can still hear the fuel pump cutting on and there is fuel spraying out the injector. <BR>The car appeared beautifull and he said it was in good shape. He would not refund my money and I couldnt even complain to ebay because I was not the high bidder but the second high bidder. The high bidder did not hold his end. Here is the link to the car  <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=557463598&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=557463598&r=0&t=0</A> <BR>Thanks for all of the responses I will keep trying||||reg||1
Z||000011||Galen||05-18-2001||06:21 PM||||damn.. pardon muh language but that man riced that sucker out.. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>and multiple little upgrades (i.e. - formula decals, "handling by lotus" fender badges, "Fiero GT" trunklid decal,18" Yellow Neon Light in back window, air cleaner painted to match car, etc.)<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>sorry to junp off subject, hehe, but whats the point of putting a formula decal and a GT decale on the same car? and I aint even gonna go there with the handling by lotus, that myth is about 88s. not 84s. THe guy you bought this car from is #1 stupid. in my humble opinion of course. I'm sure everyone here would agree. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe Auto 4Banger - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR>AIM: WookieeNC||||reg||1
Z||000012||Rex||05-18-2001||07:57 PM||||I'm sure there's some recourse on this transaction. Don't give up the ship without a fight.Two grand is a lot to sink into a car, and end up with what you are describing.<BR>Get out a little more info,ie: Is there engine oil in the air intake filter and housing? Is there excess smoke from the exhaust? ect:  hope all goes well and hope some help comes from this site. Welcome aboard!||||reg||1
