Z||000046||Taijiguy||05-20-2001||10:52 PM||||OK, throwing these thoughts out for pondering by others who might be able to diagnose the cause.<BR>If it's backfiring, and the timing is good, if it's idling OK, and only backfires when you try to accelerate, that suggests a lean condition to me. I'm not sure how the TBI compensates for acceleration. Of course a carb uses an accelerator pump. How does the TBI compensate for increased air flow? Can anyone run with my idea here?||||reg||1
